{"sections":[],"metadata":{"externalID":"s:13ShortestPaths16AStarSearchEventO","title":"AStarSearchEvent","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"AStarSearchEvent"}],"modules":[{"name":"ShortestPaths"}],"role":"symbol","symbolKind":"enum","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AStarSearchEvent","kind":"identifier"}],"remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/ShortestPaths\/AStarSearch.swift#L18","fileName":"AStarSearch.swift"},"roleHeading":"Enumeration"},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AStarSearchEvent","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Edge","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Weight","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SH","text":"Hashable","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Edge","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SH","text":"Hashable","kind":"typeIdentifier"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","level":2,"anchor":"overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The source is discovered first, at distance zero, with its estimate: the heuristic’s guess at","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"its distance to the target (zero for the target itself). Then, while a vertex is open, the one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with the smallest distance plus estimate is examined (closed). When that is the target the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"search ends there. Otherwise each of its out-edges is examined in turn with the distance it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"offers its target, the examined vertex’s distance plus the edge’s weight, and is then relaxed,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"when the offer is smaller than the target’s distance or the target was not yet discovered, or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"not relaxed. A relaxed edge to an undiscovered vertex is followed by that vertex’s discovery;","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"one to a closed vertex, which only an inconsistent heuristic allows, by its reopening (the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Boost Graph Library’s black target), after which it is examined again. After its last out-edge","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the examined vertex is finished. When the target is never reached the search ends once no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertex is open.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"relationshipsSections":[{"type":"conformsTo","kind":"relationships","title":"Conforms To","identifiers":["doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/s23CustomStringConvertibleP","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/SQ","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/s9EscapableP","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/SH","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/s16SendableMetatypeP"]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/AStarSearchEvent"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/shortestpaths\/astarsearchevent"]}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"What an A* search reports, in order, with the events of the Boost Graph Library’s A* visitor."}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths"]]},"topicSections":[{"generated":true,"title":"Enumerati